The Syntax of the .ksh Files is pretty simple:

Basics
=======

Variable --> v name = x;
Constant --> c name = x;
float --> f name = x;
int --> int name = x;

Default Actions (No Libraries Required)
========================================

Git Actions --> git.ActionToDo();
Alias Actions --> alias.ActionToDo();
Slow Actions --> slow.data();
Dir Actions --> dir.dir();
Show Input --> show();

Default Colletions (No Libraries Required)
===========================================

Prompt Structure --> prompt{}
Aliases Structure --> aliases{}
Top Prompt Structure --> topPrompt{}
Down Prompt Structure --> dPrompt{}

Colors Setters (No Libraries Required)
=======================================

Basic Colors Revalued --> basic.${Name Of The Color in The https://github.com/NickHubDev/Knight-Shell/tree/main/docs/colors/basics}();
Pre-Valuated Colors --> preColor.${Name of the Color in the https://github.com/NickHubDev/Knight-Shell/tree/main/docs/colors/perso}();

